{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124564","id":4894766512,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI8A1sA","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124564","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124564.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124564.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124564","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124564/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124564/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124564/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/a76f177b133a783f0a4fc5e6e5173e0728cf759c","number":124564,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix SDF encoder for positive endpoint","user":{"login":"BaconEggsRL","id":18596035,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NTk2MDM1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18596035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL","html_url":"https://github.com/BaconEggsRL","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BaconEggsRL/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\n\n- Closes #112926\n\n## Additional information\n\nIn canvas_sdf.glsl, float_to_vec4() encodes the signed distance into an RGBA texture.\n(p_float is the signed distance [-1,1] remapped to the range [0, 1].)\n\nThe issue is that fract() returns (0, 0, 0, 0) for both endpoints (p_float = 0 and p_float = 1).\nSo in particles.glsl, vec4_to_float() cannot determine whether (0,0,0,0) originally represented 0.0 or 1.0.\n\nvec4_to_float() decodes (0, 0, 0, 0) as -1.0, which is the maximum negative normalized distance.\nThis is interpreted as being the maximum distance inside a collider. Therefore the particles \"disappear\" to escape the collision.*\n\nWhat we want instead is for the particles to be treated as being the maximum distance away from a collider.\nThis is effectively what we do by returning (0, 0, 0, 1) instead of (0, 0, 0, 0) for positive endpoints.\n\n(*In the case of Rigid collision, I believe there is also an issue of the shader trying to normalize a zero vector. That may be a separate discussion/PR. For Hide on Contact it is more straightforward; and in any case this solution solves both issues.)\n\n## AI usage\nAI was used for investigation purposes only. I wrote the PR myself and tested everything by hand.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open"